}

Output10 20 30 Advantages of realloc()realloc() provides a convenient way to resize dynamically allocated memory while preserving existing data.It resizes an existing memory block without manually allocating and copying memory.It preserves the existing data up to the smaller of the old and new memory sizes.It can improve performance by expanding the existing memory block in place when possible.Common Mistakes While Using realloc()The following are some common mistakes that programmers should avoid while using realloc():Using realloc() on memory that was not dynamically allocated (such as stack or static memory). Not checking whether realloc() returns NULL before using the returned pointer. Assigning the result of realloc() directly to the original pointer, which may cause a memory leak if reallocation fails.
